From e4b12de12490582d60b3c57832750a9c113ea9bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SovereignOS Build <build@sovereignos.local>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:42:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] airpods: add BluetoothDevice#setAirPodsMetadata behind
 MANAGE_AIRPODS_IDENTITY

The AirPods app needs to write the metadata Settings reads for the rings and
device page. Granting it BLUETOOTH_PRIVILEGED would let it rewrite any paired
device's metadata, so add a narrow setter instead: an 18-key allow-list, only
for a device that is bonded and was registered through setAirPodsIdentity, on
the existing setMetadata storage path. The registered set is kept under one
lock shared with setAirPodsIdentity and the unbond hook so a write cannot run
after an unbond has completed. Returns true when the stored value already
equals the request, so the caller can tell refusal from no-change.
---
